            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proportional Reasoning-1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.092,
            0.847,
            0.132
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "costs 37 niskas, O expert businessman! tell me quickly what quantity of saffron can be bought for 9 niskas?”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.136,
            0.848,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Harmain is a 1-year-old girl. Her elder brother is 5 years old. What will be Harmain’s age when the ratio of her age to her brother’s age is 1 : 2?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.197,
            0.846,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. The mass of equal volumes of gold and water are in the ratio 37 : 2. If 1 litre of water is 1 kg in mass, what is the mass of 1 litre of gold?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.239,
            0.848,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. It is good farming practice to apply 10 tonnes of cow manure for 1 acre of land. A farmer is planning to grow tomatoes in a plot of size 200 ft by 500 ft. How much manure should he buy? (Please refer to the section on Unit Conversions earlier in this chapter)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.448,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.319,
            0.849,
            0.376
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. A tap takes 15 seconds to fill a mug of water. The volume of the mug is 500 mL. How much time does the same tap take to fill a bucket of water if the bucket has a 10-litre capacity?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.379,
            0.847,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. One acre of land costs ₹15,00,000. What is the cost of 2,400 square feet of the same land?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.422,
            0.849,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. A tractor can plough the same area of a field 4 times faster than a pair of oxen. A farmer wants to plough his 20-acre field. A pair of oxen takes 6 hours to plough an acre of land. How much time would it take if the farmer used a pair of oxen to plough the field? How much time would it take him if he decides to use a tractor instead?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.519,
            0.821,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. The ₹10 coin is an alloy of copper and nickel called ‘cupro-nickel’. Copper and nickel are mixed in a 3 : 1 ratio to get this alloy. The mass of the coin is 7.74 grams. If the cost of copper is ₹906 per kg and the cost of nickel is ₹1,341 per kg, what is the cost of these metals in a ₹10 coin?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.827,
            0.526,
            0.928,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.827,
                0.526,
                0.928,
                0.581
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.407,
            0.637,
            0.59,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SUMMARY"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.683,
            0.824,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ratios in the form of a : b indicate that for every ‘a’ unit of the first quantity, there are ‘b’ units of the second quantity. ‘a’ and ‘b’ are the terms in the ratio."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.746,
            0.825,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two ratios — a : b and c : d — are "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "proportional",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (written a : b :: c : d) if their terms change by the same factor, i.e., if ad = bc."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.79,
            0.821,
            0.839
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If x is divided into two parts in the ratio m : n, then the quantity of the first part is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m \\times { \\frac { x } { m + n } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the quantity of the second part is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\times { \\frac { x } { m ^ { + } n } } \\cdot"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
